  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan\u2061x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- $tan\u2061(x+\\pi )=tan\u2061(x+n\\pi ).$\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi $\n- $tan\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan\u2061(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan\u2061x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $y=tan\u2061x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan\u2061(x+\\pi )=tan\u2061(x)=tan\u2061(x+n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=tan\u2061x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan\u2061x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi )=tan\u2061(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$",
